  "content": {
    "id": "p34-q75-node",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "75",
    "prompt": "The derivative of $y=x(ax+b)^n$ is\n$$y'=(ax+b)^{n-1}h(x)$$\nfor some function $h$. Find $h(x)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$h(x)=a(n+1)x+b$.\n\nUse the product rule and factor out $(ax+b)^{n-1}$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y'&=(ax+b)^n+anx(ax+b)^{n-1}\\\\y'&=(ax+b)^{n-1}\\bigl[(ax+b)+anx\\bigr]\\\\y'&=(ax+b)^{n-1}\\bigl[a(n+1)x+b\\bigr]\\end{align*}$$\nHence $h(x)=a(n+1)x+b$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 36
  },
